From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: gate stub branch by ErrorEPC

The physical log for the PT_EPC gate shows the restore hook writing
0x80401000, then the late restore assembly seeing 0x80400108 in both CP0_EPC
and PT_EPC. At that point RESTORE_SOME has already consumed the return frame,
so the saved pt_regs EPC is not a reliable branch gate on HC15xx.

Use CP0 ErrorEPC instead. The C hook writes ErrorEPC immediately before the
restore path, and the standard MIPS RESTORE_SOME macro does not modify it.
Keep the status and EBase guards, then record marker 0x51510017 with the
ErrorEPC value before deciding whether to jump to the copied init stub.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -163,10 +163,10 @@
 	li	k0, 0x1002
 	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
-	LONG_L	k1, PT_EPC(sp)
+	MFC0	k1, CP0_ERROREPC
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
 	sw	k1, 24(k0)
-	li	k1, 0x51510016
+	li	k1, 0x51510017
 	sw	k1, 20(k0)
 	lw	k1, 24(k0)
 	sync
-- 
2.45.0
